<title>USA: Seagate to take charge for Armstrad suit.</title>
<headline>Seagate to take charge for Armstrad suit.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTS VALLEY, Calif 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagate Technology Inc said the High Court of Justice in England awarded Amstrad Plc $93 million, before interest and costs which could increase it by $60 million, resulting in a charge of a like amount to Seagate's current quarter.</p>
<p>Seagate said it make make an appeal of the decision. The Queen's Bench Division, Official Referees' Court issued its post trial order in an action entitled, Amstrad PLC v. Seagate Technology Inc and Seagate Technology Singapore PTE. Ltd. involving the 1988-1989 sales of disc drives to Amstrad.</p>
<p>A spokesperson was not immediately available.</p>
</text>
